.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
The one part of a file dialog that differs by platform\&. 

Asking for a file is the same everywhere: schultz_window\&.c takes a request number, copies what the caller asked for, and turns the answer into an event\&. Showing the dialog is not the same everywhere\&.
.PP
On Linux, Windows, macOS and Android, SDL already has a backend, and this seam is one call through to it\&. On iOS it does not: SDL 3\&.4\&.16 ships dialog backends for android, cocoa, haiku, unix and windows, its build selects the cocoa one with \fCelseif(MACOS)\fP, and iOS matches no branch at all\&. What gets compiled instead is the dummy, which is three lines that report failure without showing anything\&. That is why a file picker on iOS looked like a dialog the person dismissed the instant it opened\&.
.PP
So iOS answers here, with UIDocumentPickerViewController, and everything above this line stays the same on all six platforms\&.
.PP
\fBNot part of the host facing interface\&.\fP A host binds to \fBschultz_api\&.h\fP\&. 
.PP
Definition in file \fBschultz_files_backend\&.h\fP\&.
