.SS "typedef void(* schultz_files_answer_fn) (void *userdata, const char *const *paths, int32_t filter)"

.PP
Where a backend delivers what the person chose\&. Called exactly once for every schultz_files_show, however it ended, and possibly on a thread that is not the one the window loop runs on\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIuserdata\fP The pointer given to schultz_files_show\&. 
.br
\fIpaths\fP The chosen paths, NULL terminated, or NULL for none\&. An empty list and NULL both mean nothing was chosen; the caller treats them alike\&. 
.br
\fIfilter\fP Which filter was showing, or -1 when the platform did not say\&. 
.RE
.PP

