.SS "void schultz_files_show (\fBschultz_files_kind\fP kind, \fBSDL_Window\fP * window, const \fBschultz_file_options\fP * options, const \fBschultz_file_filter\fP * filters, uint32_t filter_count, \fBschultz_files_answer_fn\fP answer, void * userdata)"

.PP
Shows one file dialog and returns without waiting for an answer\&. The filters are the caller's copies and stay alive until after the answer arrives, so a backend may point at their strings rather than copying them again\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIkind\fP Which dialog to show\&. 
.br
\fIwindow\fP The window to hang it off\&. May be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIoptions\fP What the caller asked for, or NULL for every default\&. 
.br
\fIfilters\fP Copied filters, or NULL for none\&. 
.br
\fIfilter_count\fP How many filters there are\&. 
.br
\fIanswer\fP Called once, later, with the result\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIuserdata\fP Passed back to the callback untouched\&. 
.RE
.PP

